# Ad deliverables end with view links

A delivered ad is not delivered until the user can click it. Any reply that
hands over a spot (new, changed, or re-rendered) ENDS with a `Links` block:

- the spot's page: `https://singularitystudiosdev.github.io/superbot-ads/<spot>.html`
  (only if a per-spot page exists)
- the live capture: `https://singularitystudiosdev.github.io/superbot-ads/spot.html?spot=<name>&ratio=16:9`
- each rendered mp4: `https://singularitystudiosdev.github.io/superbot-ads/videos/<name>-<16x9|1x1|9x16>.mp4`

Full URLs with scheme — bare paths and repo-relative links don't count; the
user clicks straight into the video. Say in one word what each link is
(`16:9 render`, `live capture`). Verify with `curl -sI` (HTTP 200) before
presenting a link as live — a Pages deploy lags the push, so poll until it
lands rather than linking a 404.

Bad:  "the spot is committed and pushed."
Good: "view it: [live capture](…/spot.html?spot=board&ratio=16:9) ·
      [16:9 mp4](…/videos/board-16x9.mp4)"
